{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1784647569,"nonce":"U6My67XDAXyw9fA3CijdGKqkxMQ=","message":"## Root-cause analysis\n\nb4 discovers newer versions of a tracked series only through\n`get_extra_series()` (`src/b4/mbox.py:685`), driven by two matching\nstrategies — and neither reliably links a genuine new posting like the\nreported qualcomm series.\n\n**1. change-id path.** If the series carries an embedded `change-id:`\ntrailer (`mbox.py:716-724`), discovery issues a precise\n`nq:\"change-id: \u003ccid\u003e\"` query. Solid — but many series (especially those\nnot generated by `b4 prep`) have no change-id at all.\n\n**2. subject+from fallback.** With no change-id (`by_changeid=False`), it\nfalls back to `(s:\"\u003csubject\u003e\" AND f:\"\u003cemail\u003e\")` (`mbox.py:757-760`).\npublic-inbox's `s:` matches subject *terms*; if the resubmission reworded\nthe subject at all (common between versions), the term set differs and the\nnew posting simply isn't returned. The new version is invisible.\n\nEven when discovery *does* surface candidates, associating them back to a\ntracked series happens by change-id, and without a real one b4 synthesizes\n`{date}-{slug}-{fingerprint[:12]}` (`src/b4/review/tracking.py:566-570`).\nTwo postings of the \"same\" series that differ in subject, date, or\npatch-ids get *different* synthesized change-ids and never collapse into a\nsingle series — `find_existing_change_id()`\n(`review/tracking.py:1097-1120`) keys on fingerprint / message-id /\nchange-id, all of which differ across a legitimately new version.\n\n**Net:** for a series without an embedded change-id, b4 has no durable\nidentity on which to hang a \"this is vN+1 of that\" relationship, and the\nsubject heuristic is best-effort by nature (\"never going to be 100%\", as\nMark notes).\n\n## Related bugs\n\nThis is the *false-negative* face of the identity gap. Bug `78c0fa1` is the\n*false-positive* face — the same subject+from fallback matching two\n*unrelated* series. `2235355` is the older-version variant; `08646dc` is\nthe upgrade UX once a newer version is known. The 0.16 \"manual revision\nlinking\" feature (`absorb_series_as_revision()` + the TUI link action) is\nthe deliberate escape hatch for exactly this: it lets the human assert the\nlink the heuristic cannot infer.","files":null}]}